jobs.description:
Originally**founded in 1991**as Harlem RBI, DREAM has grown to annually serve more than 2,500 youth across East Harlem and the South Bronx through a network of seven PreK-12, extended-day, extended-year DREAM Charter Schools and community sports-based youth development programs. Through our **commitment** to rigorous academics, social-emotional learning, deep family and community engagement, and health and wellness, we create lifelong learners who are equipped to fulfill their vision of success in and out of the classroom. We dream big, as well, with an aggressive five-year plan to expand to serve 3,500 students across **seven schools**—growing our **organization’s impact** and leveling the playing field for all children. To learn more, visit **wearedream.org****.**

DREAM seeks an **Advancement Operations Coordinator** (posted as **Development Coordinator**) to join our Advancement team. Reporting to the Senior Director of Advancement Operations, this role provides administrative, operational, and project coordination support across the Advancement department. The Advancement Operations Coordinator serves as a key partner to Advancement leadership and works closely with the Director of Special Events, Advancement Operations Manager, Special Events Manager, Annual Fund Manager, Database Manager, and frontline fundraisers to support the day-to-day operations that enable fundraising success.

This is an exciting opportunity for a highly organized, detail-oriented professional who enjoys coordinating projects, managing multiple priorities, and building strong relationships across teams. The ideal candidate is proactive, collaborative, and eager to grow within nonprofit fundraising and Advancement Operations.

### **Responsibilities**

**Fundraising Operations**

* Support routine Salesforce updates, donor activity tracking, and portfolio administration in partnership with the Database Manager and Advancement Operations Manager;
* Coordinate logistics for portfolio review meetings, fundraising planning sessions, and other recurring Advancement meetings;
* Draft routine donor correspondence, stewardship communications, acknowledgments, and other donor engagement materials, as assigned;
* Support the preparation and distribution of donor meeting materials, prospect briefings, and stewardship resources.

**Advancement Operations**

* Coordinate Advancement department meetings, planning sessions, retreats, and other departmental activities, including scheduling, agendas, meeting materials, note-taking, and follow-up;
* Maintain departmental calendars, shared resources, operational documentation, and other administrative tools that support the efficient day-to-day functioning of the Advancement team;
* Coordinate cross-functional operational workstreams and support departmental operations, including purchasing, vendor coordination, invoice processing, expense reconciliation, team recognition activities, and other administrative functions;
* Partner with the Database Manager to support routine Salesforce updates, maintain accurate fundraising records, assist with donor lists and mail merges, and identify data inconsistencies for review;
* Provide administrative support for departmental reporting, process improvements, and special projects that strengthen Advancement operations.

**Events & Campaign Support**

* Support the planning and execution of fundraising events, donor stewardship activities, volunteer engagement initiatives, and Annual Fund campaigns in partnership with the Director of Special Events, Special Events Manager, and Annual Giving Manager;
* Coordinate event registrations, guest communications, event materials, volunteer logistics, and other operational needs for Advancement events;
* Assist with post-event follow-up, stewardship activities, and administrative support related to fundraising campaigns and donor engagement initiatives.

Other responsibilities as assigned.

### **Qualifications**

* Bachelor's degree, required;
* One to three years of experience in nonprofit development/fundraising operations, internships and relevant volunteer experience will be considered;
* Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities;
* Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills;
* Experience coordinating meetings, calendars, projects, or events in a fast-paced environment;
* Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues across departments and with external stakeholders;
* Strong problem-solving skills and a proactive, customer-service-oriented approach;
* Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google Workspace;
* Experience with Salesforce or another CRM, preferred;
* Interest in building a career in nonprofit fundraising, advancement, or operations;
* A strong belief in the mission and values of DREAM, including the belief that all students can succeed and a deep desire to make a difference in the lives of our students, families, and community.

### **Working Expectations**

* This role is part of the Advancement Team, which currently works 3 days in the office and up to 2 days remote, per week (subject to change, and with some weeks requiring more time in-person, for example for donor events).
* Some evening and/or weekend work, for example to prepare for and attend donor events, is required.

### **Benefits and Paid Time Off**

